title: Genesis 8 – While the Earth Remaineth
description: A study in Genesis 8: the waters abate, Noah’s sacrifice of thanksgiving, and God’s promise that seedtime and harvest shall not cease.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-8-while-the-earth-remaineth.html

=== Introduction
--- While the Earth Remaineth [title]
overline: A study in Genesis 8
sub: The waters abate, Noah gives thanks, and God promises to preserve the world until the end.
refs: Genesis 8:1-5; Genesis 8:20-22
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== The waters abate
--- God remembered Noah
scripture: Genesis 8:1-3 | mark: God remembered Noah; The fountains also of the deep and the windows of heaven were stopped
p: Noah and his ark of survivors ride out the flood, and the deluge abates, as God closes up the windows of heaven and the fountains of the deep. [[Genesis 7:11]]

--- The ark rested
scripture: Genesis 8:4-5 | mark: upon the mountains of Ararat
p: The final resting place for the ark, in Turkey: Mt. Ararat. So many “In Search Of”s and History channel specials claim to have found the ark, but we know everything we need to from scripture.

--- A hard record of events
stat: 17th | day of the 2nd month, the rain began [[Genesis 7:11]]
stat: 17th | day of the 7th month, the ark rested [[Genesis 8:4]]
stat: 601 | Noah’s age, the 1st day of the 1st month [[Genesis 8:13]]
stat: 27th | day of the 2nd month, the earth was dried [[Genesis 8:14]]
p: The times given are details that mark this account as historical rather than symbolic or allegory. God rarely gives precise measures of time or place unless it is to create a hard record of events in scripture. Noah’s 601st birthday is marked while waiting to get God’s blessing to disembark.

--- The raven and the dove
scripture: Genesis 8:6-12 | mark: in her mouth was an olive leaf pluckt off
p: The raven and the doves sent by Noah, and the olive branch the dove returns with, are taught in every Sunday school: that God offered an olive branch of peace to mankind. It reads a bit more into it than is there, but maybe. Nothing is incidental, accidental or coincidental in scripture.

--- Go forth of the ark
scripture: Genesis 8:15-19 | mark: Go forth of the ark
center: Noah waited on God’s word to go in, and he waited on God’s word to come out. [[Genesis 7:1]] [[Genesis 7:16]]

=== A sweet savour
--- Noah builded an altar
scripture: Genesis 8:20 | mark: of every clean beast, and of every clean fowl
p: Noah settled in, the ark unloaded, makes sacrifice to God. An act of incredible faith, given the limited number of animals to survive the flood, and it is pleasing unto God.
note: This is why Noah took the clean beasts by sevens. [[Genesis 7:2-3]]

--- The Lord said in his heart
heading: The {Lord} said in his heart
big: Genesis 8:21 | mark: the imagination of man’s heart is evil from his youth
p: God gives us insight to His thought process, recognizing the evil imagination within man’s heart, and vows never to destroy every living thing because of it. Rather than curse the ground and total destruction of life, God vows to preserve the world as is until the end. [[Genesis 6:5]]

=== While the earth remaineth
--- Seedtime and harvest shall not cease [title]
overline: Genesis 8:22
big: Genesis 8:22 | mark: shall not cease

--- No cause for panic
lead: This is why environmentalist panic is unbiblical nonsense. We are not going to see cataclysmic climate change of any type before the day of the {Lord}.
panel: God keeps the seasons | Seedtime and harvest, cold and heat, summer and winter, day and night shall not cease while the earth remaineth.
panel-warn: Foolish cope | I wonder sometimes if the entire point of climate panic is to make those alive during the tribulation and into the wrath of God doubt His hand in it. There probably will be some deluded souls, even as the locusts of Hell bite them in the darkness, blaming CO₂ emissions. [[Revelation 9:2-6]]
center: We will see the covenant God gives Noah in Genesis 9. [[lesson:genesis-9-blessings-and-covenant|Genesis 9]]

=== Close
--- God remembered Noah [title]
overline: Genesis 8
sub: and He keeps His word to the end.
point: The flood was history | Days, months and years, and a mountain named. A hard record, not allegory.
point: Faith gives thanks | Noah’s first act on dry ground was an altar, and it was a sweet savour unto the {Lord}.

--- God remembered Noah, continued
point: God preserves the world | Not because man is good, for his heart is evil from his youth, but because God has promised.
point: Fear God, not man’s panic | While the earth remaineth, seedtime and harvest shall not cease.

